The lexicon of Lojban is unbounded (thanks to lujvo and le'avla/fu'ivla)
but in any case, we can assume that it is large enough that the number
of cmavo is irrelevant in that respect (which doesn't mean that I wouldn't
get rid of quite a few of them, but that's another discussion).
 
As for (b), if scrapping the semantico-syntactic rules relevant to {kau}
simplifies the grammar, so would doing the same thing with respect to {pa}.
 
